# GCE v2.0 — Universal Music Evaluation Standard

**Index:** `docs/GCE_CANONICAL.md` (live sources + parked legacy list).

GCE has **two agent modes**. Pick the right one before scoring or advising.

## Mode selection

| Mode | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| **Formal / technical** | Editing or reviewing Composer OS code · running the official GCE evaluator (`gceStyleEval`, eval scripts, smoke harness) · LOCK / DCR / hard gates / quality gates · release readiness or CI pass/fail · interpreting **automated** scores from the system |
| **Musician-facing / conversational** | Mike asks in chat: “GCE this”, “GCE score”, “evaluate this piece”, “is this good?”, “pros and cons?”, “what would raise it?” — **unless** he explicitly asks for formal Composer OS validation |

**Default mode:** Unless the prompt asks for **formal Composer OS validation** or mentions **LOCK**, **DCR**, or **CI**, use **musician-facing** GCE for chat evaluation. Use **formal / technical** GCE for pipeline work (code, evaluator runs, release readiness).

---

## 1. Formal / technical GCE (strict gate mode)

Every time Composer OS **generates MusicXML output** or you **run the official evaluator**, use formal GCE only.

- Hard gates remain hard gates; formulas, weights, and thresholds are authoritative and **unchanged**
- **9.0** = aspirational north star · **7.9–8.4** = current empirical release-quality band
- Short-form caveats below still apply
- Do **not** weaken or reinterpret formal GCE / LOCK semantics in this mode

Full framework: see docs/GCE_FRAMEWORK_V2.md

**Integrated standards (GCE + LOCK + DCR + Style Profile Layer):** `docs/GCE_LOCK_DCR_STANDARDS.md`  
**Pre-commit / workflow / per-slice rules:** `.cursor/rules/composer-os-quality-gates.mdc`

Quick reference:
- 10 categories, all score 0-10
- **9.0** = aspirational north star (long-term benchmark; formulas unchanged)
- **7.9–8.4** = current empirical release-quality / system-ceiling band (tuned, shipped-quality output under the present system)
- **Operational release band:** >= 7.9 PASS · 6.5–7.8 acceptable / promising / one weakest-category pass · < 6.5 materially weak / investigate
- If below release band: revise weakest only, one pass, no full rewrite (DCR)
- **Hard gates remain true blockers** regardless of calibrated overall band (auto-fail):
  - Melodic Identity <= 6
  - No section contrast
  - Cadential Clarity coverage < 0.4
  - Final bar tension > 0.7 (accidental / unresolved ending)

### Short-form / fragment outputs (< ~16 bars, especially 8-bar leadsheet)

Do **not** judge fragments the same way as full-chart output. Some categories are **structurally limited** on short material:
- **thematicRecallPotential**, **structureAndForm**, parts of **phraseGrammar** — report as structurally limited / N/A-leaning / interpret with caution; not automatic craft failure
- **rhythmAntiLoop**, **harmony & language / chord fidelity**, **range / idiomaticity** — still meaningful on short-form; low scores here may be real findings
- A **5.x** short-form score is **not** release quality; it may mix real underperformance **and** measurement distortion — triage before recommending deep composer-grammar work

### Roadmap triage (low GCE on leadsheet / short-form)

1. Ask whether the score is distorted by short-form limits  
2. Prioritize **>8-bar / full-chart** evaluation before deep architectural craft work  
3. Only after fair full-chart scoring, recommend large-scale composer-behavioural-grammar work  
4. Immediate fixable findings on short-form still matter: rhythmAntiLoop / too-perfect grid, chord-fidelity bugs, range / idiomaticity bugs  

Apply **formal** GCE whenever:
- Generating or evaluating Composer OS MusicXML output
- Running gceStyleEval or any evaluation script
- Changing composer slices, Song Mode style surfaces, ECM/vault layers, or export paths (also satisfy LOCK + Style Profile Layer in `docs/GCE_LOCK_DCR_STANDARDS.md`)

